      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>Der-\u1e25ud\u016bd-i Filis\u1e6d\u012bn</em>:\u00a0It is a large district, within which lie <em>Beyt\u00fc\u2019l-ma\u1e33dis</em> (Jerusalem), <em>\u0120azze</em> (Gaza), and <em>\u2018As\u1e33al\u0101n</em> (Ashkelon).\u00a0Its western boundary runs from <em>Refa\u1e25</em> (Rafah) to <em>Lecc\u016bn</em> (Legio), and its width is two days\u2019 journey, extending from <em>Y\u0101f\u0101</em> (Jaffa) to <em>Er\u012b\u1e25\u0101</em> (Jericho).\u00a0At present, <em>Zu\u0121ar</em>, the diy\u0101r-\u0131 L\u016b\u1e6d (the region of Lot, i.e., around the Dead Sea), as well as <em>Cib\u0101l</em>\u00a0and <em>\u015eerr\u0101n</em> (the Sharon plain) are all attached to <em>Filis\u1e6d\u012bn</em> (Palestine).\u00a0Its water comes from rainfall, except in <em>N\u0101blus</em> (Nablus), where there is running water.\u00a0And the great cities of this <em>\u2018\u00f6rf\u012b</em> (customary administrative) district are <em>Beyt-i Ma\u1e33dis</em> (Jerusalem), <em>\u0120azze</em> (Gaza), and <em>Remle</em> (Ramla).\u00a0All\u0101h knows the best. [translation]</p>",
